4. Place vos mains in front of you as you reach le sol. This movement is very difficult and you may be unable to do it unaided. Use vos bras to lightly push off le sol to aid your Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Floor_Glute-Ham_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Floor Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Adjust the j-hooks so they are at the appropriate height to rack the bar. Begin lying on le sol with votre tête near the end of a power rack. Keeping your omoplates pulled together; pull the bar off of the hooks.
2. Lower the bar towards the bottom of your poitrine or upper stomach, squeezing the bar and attempting to pull it apart as you do so. Ensure that you tuck your coudes throughout le mouvement. Lower the bar until your upper arm contacts the ground and pause, preventing any slamming or bouncing of the poids.
3. Press the bar back up as fast as you can, keeping the bar, your poignets, and coudes in line as you do so.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Floor_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Floor Press with Chains', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Adjust the j-hooks so they are at the appropriate height to rack the bar. For cet exercice, drape the chains directly over the end of the bar, trying to keep the ends away from the plates.
2. Begin lying on le sol with votre tête near the end of a power rack. Keeping your omoplates pulled together, pull the bar off of the hooks.
3. Lower the bar towards the bottom of your poitrine or upper stomach, squeezing the bar and attempting to pull it apart as you do so. Ensure that you tuck your coudes throughout le mouvement. Lower the bar until your upper arm contacts the ground and pause, preventing any slamming or bouncing of the poids.
4. Press the bar back up as fast as you can, keeping the bar, your poignets, and coudes in line as you do so.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Floor_Press_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Flutter Kicks', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. On a flat banc lie facedown with the hanches on the edge of the banc, the legs straight with toes high off le sol and with the arms on top of the banc holding on to the front edge.
2. Squeeze your fessiers and ischio-jambiers and straighten the legs until they are level with the hanches. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Start le mouvement by lifting the left leg higher than the right leg.
4. Then lower the left leg as you lift the right leg.
5. Continue alternating in this manner (as though you are doing a flutter kick in water) until you have done the recommended amount of repetitions for each leg. Make sure that you keep a controlled movement en permanence. Conseil : You will breathe normally as you perform this movement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Flutter_Kicks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Foot-SMR', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. cet exercice stretches the fascia of the muscles in the feet. Start off seated with your shoes removed. Using a foot roller or a similar object, such as a small section of pvc pipe, place your foot against the roller across the arch of your foot. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Press down firmly, rolling across the arch of your foot. Maintenez 10-30 secondes, and then switch feet.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Foot-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Forward Drag with Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Attach a dual handled chain or rope attachment to the sled. You should be facing away from the sled, holding a handle in each hand.
2. Begin le mouvement by moving forward for one step. Leaning forward, extend through the legs and hanches to move, pausing with each step to extend through the coudes, pressing vos mains forward. Step forward until you return to the start position prepared to press.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Forward_Drag_with_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Frankenstein Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This drill teaches you the proper positioning of both the bar and votre corps during the clean and front squat.
2. Place the barre on the front of the épaules, releasing your grip and extending vos bras out in front of you. The épaules should be pushed forward to create a shelf, and the bar should be in contact with the throat. Ensure that you only move your omoplates forward; don''t round the thoracic spine.
3. Squat by flexing the genous and hanches, sitting in between vos jambes. Keep the torse upright, the arms up, and the épaules forward, and the bar should stay in place. Go to the bottom of the squat, until your ischio-jambiers contact your mollets.
4. Return to the upright position by driving through the front of the heel and extending the genous and hanches.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Frankenstein_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Freehand Jump Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Cross vos bras over your poitrine.
2. With votre tête up and votre dos straight, position vos pieds at épaule width.
3. Keeping votre dos straight and poitrine up, squat down as you inspirez until your upper cuisses are parallel, or lower, to le sol.
4. Now pressing mainly with the ball of vos pieds, jump straight up in the air as high as possible, using the cuisses like springs. Expirez during this portion of le mouvement.
5. When you touch le sol again, immediately squat down and jump again.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Freehand_Jump_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Frog Hops', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos mains behind votre tête, and squat down keeping your torse upright and votre tête up. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Jump forward several feet, avoiding jumping unnecessarily high. As vos pieds contact the ground, absorb the impact through vos jambes, and jump again. Répétez this action 5-10 times.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Frog_Hops/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Frog Sit-Ups', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Lie with votre dos flat on le sol (or exercise mat) and vos jambes extended in front of you.
2. Now bend at the genous and place your outer cuisses by le sol (or mat) as you make the soles of vos pieds touch each other.
3. Now try pushing both soles and bringing them up as near you as possible while you keep the outer cuisses on le sol (or at least almost touching it). Conseil : In this position vos jambes should create a diamond shape.
4. Now, cross vos bras in front of you by touching the opposite épaules. C''est votre position de départ.
5. As you expirez flatten your lower back to le sol while curling the torse upwards. Conseil : This will be like performing the first 1/4 movement of a sit up. Hold at the top position for a second.
6. As you inspirez, Lentement, lower back to the position de départ.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Frog_Sit-Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Barbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, bring vos bras up under the bar while keeping the coudes high and the upper arm slightly above parallèle au sol. Rest the bar on top of the deltoids and cross vos bras while grasping the bar for total control.
2. Lift the bar off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances described in the foot positioning section).
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol mainly with the middle of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Barbell Squat To A Bench', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set a flat banc behind you and set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, bring vos bras up under the bar while keeping the coudes high and the upper arm slightly above parallèle au sol. Rest the bar on top of the deltoids and cross vos bras while grasping the bar for total control.
2. Lift the bar off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances described in the foot positioning section).
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you touch the banc with your fessiers. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol mainly with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Barbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Box Jump', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Begin with a box of an appropriate height 1-2 feet in front of you. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds should width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Perform a short squat in preparation for jumping, swinging vos bras behind you.
3. Rebound out of this position, extending through the hanches, genous, and chevilles to jump as high as possible. Swing vos bras forward and up.
4. Land on the box with the genous bent, absorbing the impact through the legs. You can jump from the box back to the ground, or preferably step down one leg at a time.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Box_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Cable Raise', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Select the poids on a low pulley machine and grasp the single hand cable attachment that is attached to the low pulley with your left hand.
2. Face away from the pulley and put your arm straight down with the hand cable attachment in front of your cuisses at arms'' length with the palms of the hand facing your cuisses. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While maintaining the torse stationary (no swinging), lift the left arm to the front with a slight bend on the coude and the palms of the hand always faces down. Continue to go up until you arm is slightly above parallèle au sol. Expirez as you execute this portion of le mouvement and pause for a second at the top.
4. Now as you inspirez lower the arm back down Lentement, to the position de départ.
5. Once all of the recommended amount of repetitions have been performed for this arm, switch arms and perform the exercise with the right one.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Cable_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Cone Hops (or hurdle hops)', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Set up a row of cones or other small barriers, placing them a few feet apart.
2. Stand in front of the first cone with vos pieds épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by jumping with both feet over the first cone, swinging both arms as you jump.
4. Absorb the impact of landing by bending the genous, rebounding out of the first leap by jumping over the next cone.
5. Continue until you have jumped over all of the cones.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Cone_Hops_or_hurdle_hops/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Dumbbell Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a couple of haltères and Tenez-vous debout avec a straight torse and the haltères on front of your cuisses bras tendus with the palms of the hand facing your cuisses. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While maintaining the torse stationary (no swinging), lift the left haltère to the front with a slight bend on the coude and the palms of the hands always facing down. Continue to go up until you arm is slightly above parallèle au sol. Expirez as you execute this portion of le mouvement and pause for a second at the top. Inspirez after the second pause.
3. Now lower the haltère back down Lentement, to the position de départ as you simultaneously lift the right haltère.
4. Continue alternating in this fashion until all of the recommended amount of repetitions have been performed for each arm.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Incline Dumbbell Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with the incline set anywhere between 30 to 60 degrees while holding a haltère on each hand. Conseil : You can change the angle to hit the muscle a little differently each time.
2. Extend vos bras straight in front of you and have your paumes vers down with the haltères raised about 1 inch above your cuisses. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, raise the haltères straight up until they are slightly above your épaules, while keeping your coudes locked. Squeeze at the top for a second and make sure you Expirez during this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep votre tête resting down against the banc and vos jambes on le sol en permanence.
4. Lower the arms back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Incline_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Leg Raises', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand next to a chair or other support, holding on with one hand.
2. Swing your leg forward, keeping the leg straight. Continue with a downward swing, bringing the leg as far back as your flexibility allows. Répétez 5-10 times, and then switch legs.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Leg_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Plate Raise', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. While standing straight, hold a barre plate in both hands at the 3 and 9 o''clock positions. Your palms should be facing each other and vos bras should be extended and locked with a slight bend at the coudes and the plate should be down near your waist in front of you as far as you can go. Conseil : The arms will remain in this position throughout the exercise. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lentement, raise the plate as you expirez until it is a little above épaule level. Hold the contraction for a second. Conseil : make sure that you do not swing the poids or bend at the coudes. Your torse should remain stationary throughout le mouvement as well.
3. As you inspirez, Lentement, lower the plate back down to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Plate_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Raise And Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat while holding a barre using a palms down grip that is about 15 inches apart.
2. Place the bar on your upper cuisses, extend vos bras and lock them while keeping a slight bend on the coudes. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now raise the poids using a semicircular motion and keeping vos bras straight as you inspirez. Continue the same movement until the bar is on the other side above votre tête . (Conseil : the bar will travel approximately 180-degrees). At this point vos bras should be parallèle au sol with the palms of vos mains facing the ceiling.
4. Now return the barre to the position de départ by reversing the motion as you expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Raise_And_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Squat (Clean Grip)', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. To begin, first set the bar in a rack slightly below épaule level. Rest the bar on top of the deltoids, pushing into the clavicles, and lightly touching the throat. vos mains should be in a clean grip, touching the bar only with your fingers to help keep it in position.
2. Lift the bar off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête and coudes up en permanence. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Bend at the genous, sitting down between vos jambes. Continue down until your ischio-jambiers are on your mollets. Keep your genous aligned with vos pieds by consciously using your abductors to push your genous out as you squat.
4. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol mainly with the heel or middle of your foot as you straighten the legs again and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Squat_Clean_Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Squats With Two Kettlebells', 'Quadriceps', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your épaules. Clean the kettlebells to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebells towards your épaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so.
2. Looking straight ahead en permanence, squat as low as you can and pause at the bottom. As you squat down, push your genous out. You should squat between vos jambes, keeping an upright torse, with votre tête and poitrine up.
3. Rise back up by driving through your heels and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Squats_With_Two_Kettlebells/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Front Two-Dumbbell Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a couple of haltères and Tenez-vous debout avec a straight torse and the haltères on front of your cuisses bras tendus with the palms of the hand facing your cuisses. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While maintaining the torse stationary (no swinging), lift the haltères to the front with a slight bend on the coude and the palms of the hands always facing down. Continue to go up until you arms are slightly above parallèle au sol. Expirez as you execute this portion of le mouvement and pause for a second at the top.
3. As you inspirez, lower the haltères back down Lentement, to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Front_Two-Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Full Range-Of-Motion Lat Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Either standing or seated on a high banc, grasp two stirrup cables that are attached to the high pulleys. Grab with the opposing hand so vos bras are crisscrossed about you and your palms are facing forward.
2. Keeping your poitrine up and maintaining a slight arch in your lower back, pull the handles down as if you were doing a regular pulldown. The range of motion will be more of an arc. During le mouvement, rotate vos mains so that in the bottom position your palms face each other rather than forward. Return Lentement, to the position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Full_Range-Of-Motion_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Gironda Sternum Chins', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grasp the pull-up bar with a épaule width prise en supination.
2. Now hang with vos bras fully extended and stick your poitrine out and lean back. Conseil : You will be leaning back throughout the entire movement. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Start pulling yourself towards the bar with your spine arched throughout le mouvement and votre tête leaning back as far away from the bar as possible. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : At the upper end of le mouvement, your hanches and legs will be at about a angle de 45 degrés to le sol.
4. Keep pulling until your collarbone passes the bar and your lower poitrine or sternum area touches it. Hold that contraction for a second. Conseil : By the time you''ve completed this portion of le mouvement; votre tête will be parallèle au sol.
5. Lentement, start going back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Gironda_Sternum_Chins/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Glute Ham Raise', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Begin by adjusting the equipment to fit votre corps. Place vos pieds against the footplate in between the rollers as you lie facedown. Your genous should be just behind the pad.
2. Start from the bottom of le mouvement. Keep votre dos arched as you begin le mouvement by flexing the genous. Drive your toes into the foot plate as you do so. Keep your upper body straight, and continue until votre corps is upright.
3. Revenez en position de départ, keeping your descent under control.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Glute_Ham_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Glute Kickback', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Mettez-vous à genoux or an exercise mat and bend at the waist with vos bras extended in front of you (perpendiculaire à the torse) in order to get into a kneeling push-up position but with the arms spaced at épaule width. votre tête should be looking forward and the bend of the genous should create a angle de 90 degrés between the ischio-jambiers and the mollets. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you expirez, lift up your right leg until the ischio-jambiers are in line with the back while maintaining the angle de 90 degrés bend. Contract the fessiers throughout this movement and hold the contraction at the top for a second. Conseil : At the end of le mouvement the upper leg should be parallèle au sol while the calf should be perpendiculaire à it.
3. Go back to the initial position as you inspirez and now Répétez with the left leg.
4. Continue to alternate legs until all of the recommended repetitions have been performed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Glute_Kickback/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Goblet Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Kettlebell', '1. Stand holding a light kettlebell by the horns close to your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Squat down between vos jambes until your ischio-jambiers are on your mollets. Keep your poitrine and head up and votre dos straight.
3. At the bottom position, pause and use your coudes to push your genous out. Revenez en position de départ, and Répétez for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Goblet_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Good Morning', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar on a rack at épaule height. Rack the bar across the rear of your épaules as you would a power squat, not on top of your épaules. Keep votre dos tight, omoplates pinched together, and your genous slightly bent. Step back from the rack.
2. Begin by bending at the hanches, moving them back as you bend over to near parallel. Keep votre dos arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.
3. Reverse the motion by extending through the hanches with your fessiers and ischio-jambiers. Continue until you have returned to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Good_Morning/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Good Morning off Pins', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar on a rack at about the same height as your stomach. Bend over underneath the bar and rack the bar across the rear of your épaules as you would a power squat, not on top of your épaules. At the proper height, you should be near parallèle au sol when bent over. Keep votre dos tight, omoplates pinched together, and your genous slightly bent. Keep votre dos arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.
2. Begin the motion by extending through the hanches with your fessiers and ischio-jambiers, and you are standing with the poids. Lentement, lower the poids back to the pins returning to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Good_Morning_off_Pins/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Gorilla Chin/Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Hang from a chin-up bar using an prise en supination (paumes vers you) that is slightly wider than épaule width.
2. Now bend your genous at a angle de 90 degrés so that the mollets are parallèle au sol while the cuisses remain perpendiculaire à it. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you expirez, pull yourself up while crunching your genous up at the same time until your genous are at poitrine level. You will stop going up as soon as your nose is at the same level as the bar. Conseil : When you get to this point you should also be finishing the crunch at the same time.
4. Lentement, start to inspirez as you Revenez en position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Gorilla_Chin_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Groin and Back Stretch', 'Adducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Asseyez-vous au sol with your genous bent and feet together.
2. Interlock your fingers behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Curl downwards, bringing your coudes to the inside of your cuisses. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ with votre tête up and votre dos straight. Répétez for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Groin_and_Back_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Groiners', 'Adducteurs', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a pushup position on le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Using both legs, jump forward landing with vos pieds next to vos mains. Keep votre tête up as you do so.
3. Revenez en position de départ and immediately Répétez le mouvement, continuing for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Groiners/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hack Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. Place the back of your torse against the back pad of the machine and hook your épaules under the épaule pads provided.
2. Position vos jambes in the platform using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Conseil : Keep votre tête up en permanence and also maintain the back on the pad en permanence.
3. Place vos bras on the side handles of the machine and disengage the safety bars (which on most designs is done by moving the side handles from a facing front position to a diagonal position).
4. Now straighten vos jambes without locking the genous. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances described in the foot positioning section).
5. Begin to Lentement, lower the unit by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up (back on the pad en permanence). Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
6. Begin to raise the unit as you expirez by pushing le sol with mainly with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hack_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hammer Curls', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright and a haltère on each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse.
2. The palms of the hands should be facing your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now, while holding your upper arm stationary, expirez and curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps. Continue to raise the poids until the biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltère is at épaule level. Hold the contracted position for a brief moment as you squeeze the biceps. Conseil : Focus on keeping the coude stationary and only moving your forearm.
4. After the brief pause, inspirez and Lentement, begin the lower the haltères back down to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hammer_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hammer Grip Incline DB Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on an incline banc with a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. By using your cuisses to help you get the haltères up, clean the haltères one arm at a time so that you can hold them at épaule width.
3. Once at épaule width, keep the palms of vos mains with a neutral grip (paumes vers each other). Keep your coudes flared out with the upper arms in line with the épaules (perpendiculaire à the torse) and the coudes bent creating a angle de 90 degrés between the upper arm and the forearm. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Now bring down the poids Lentement, to your side as you Inspirez. Keep full control of the haltères en permanence.
5. As you Expirez, push the haltères up using your pectoral muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down slowly. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
7. When you are done, place the haltères back in your cuisses and then on le sol. This is the safest manner to dispose of the haltères.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hammer_Grip_Incline_DB_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hamstring-SMR', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Foam roller', '1. In a seated position, extend vos jambes over a foam roll so that it is position on the back of the upper legs. Place vos mains to the side or behind you to help support your poids. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Using vos mains, lift your hanches off of le sol and shift your poids on the foam roll to one leg. Relax the ischio-jambiers of the leg you are stretching.
3. Roll over the foam from below the hanche to above the back of the genou, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hamstring-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hamstring Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with one leg extended above you, with the hanche at ninety degrees. Keep the other leg flat on le sol.
2. Loop a belt, band, or rope over the ball of your foot. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull on the belt to create tension in the mollets and ischio-jambiers. Hold this stretch for 10-30 seconds, and Répétez with the other leg.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Handstand Push-Ups', 'Épaules', 'Poids de corps', '1. With votre dos to the wall bend at the waist and place both hands on le sol at épaule width.
2. Kick yourself up against the wall with vos bras straight. votre corps should be upside down with the arms and legs fully extended. Keep your whole body as straight as possible. Conseil : If doing this for the first time, have a spotter help you. Also, make sure that you keep facing the wall with votre tête, rather than looking down.
3. Lentement, lower yourself to the ground as you inspirez until votre tête almost touches le sol. Conseil : It is of utmost importance that you come down slow in order to avoid head injury.
4. Push yourself back up Lentement, as you expirez until your coudes are nearly locked.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Handstand_Push-Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hang Clean', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a épaule width, double overhand or hook grip, with the bar hanging at the mid cuisse position. votre dos should be straight and inclined slightly forward.
2. Begin by aggressively extending through the hanches, genous and chevilles, driving the poids upward. As you do so, shrug your épaules towards your ears.
3. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hang_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hang Clean - Below the Knees', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a épaule width, double overhand or hook grip, with the bar hanging just below the genous. votre dos should be straight and inclined slightly forward.
2. Begin by aggressively extending through the hanches, genous and chevilles, driving the poids upward. As you do so, shrug your épaules towards your ears. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out.
3. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.
4. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hang_Clean_-_Below_the_Knees/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hang Snatch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a prise large on the bar, with an overhand or hook grip. The feet should be directly below the hanches with the feet turned out. Your genous should be slightly bent, and the torse inclined forward. The spine should be fully extended and the head facing forward. The bar should be at the hanches. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Aggressively extend through the legs and hanches. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
3. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.
4. Return to a standing position with the poids overhead. Follow by returning the poids to the ground under control.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hang_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hang Snatch - Below Knees', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a prise large on the bar, with an overhand or hook grip. The feet should be directly below the hanches with the feet turned out. Your genous should be slightly bent, and the torse inclined forward. The spine should be fully extended and the head facing forward. The bar should be just below the genous. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Aggressively extend through the legs and hanches. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
3. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.
4. Return to a standing position with the poids overhead, and then return the poids to le sol under control.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hang_Snatch_-_Below_Knees/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hanging Bar Good Morning', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar on a rack at about the same height as your stomach. Suspend the bar using chains or suspension straps.
2. Bend over underneath the bar and rack the bar across the rear of your épaules as you would a power squat, not on top of your traps. At the proper height, you should be near parallèle au sol when bent over. Keep votre dos tight, omoplates pinched together, and your genous slightly bent. Keep votre dos arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.
3. Begin the motion by extending through the hanches with your fessiers and ischio-jambiers, and you are standing with the poids.
4. Lentement, lower the poids back to the position de départ, where it is supported by the chains.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hanging_Bar_Good_Morning/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hanging Leg Raise', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Hang from a chin-up bar with both arms extended bras tendus in top of you using either a prise large or a prise moyenne. The legs should be straight down with the pelvis rolled slightly backwards. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise vos jambes until the torse makes a angle de 90 degrés with the legs. Expirez as you perform this movement and hold the contraction for a second or so.
3. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hanging_Leg_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hanging Pike', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Hang from a chin-up bar with vos jambes and feet together using an prise en pronation (paumes vers away from you) that is slightly wider than épaule width. Conseil : You may use poignet wraps in order to facilitate holding on to the bar.
2. Now bend your genous at a angle de 90 degrés and bring the upper legs forward so that the mollets are perpendiculaire à le sol while the cuisses remain parallel to it. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull vos jambes up as you expirez until you almost touch your shins with the bar above you. Conseil : Try to straighten vos jambes as much as possible while at the top.
4. Lower vos jambes as Lentement, as possible until you reach the position de départ. Conseil : Avoid swinging and using momentum en permanence.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hanging_Pike/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Heaving Snatch Balance', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This drill helps you learn the snatch. Begin by holding a light poids across the back of the épaules. vos pieds should be slightly wider than hanche width apart with the feet turned out, the same position that you would perform a squat with.
2. Begin by dipping with the genous slightly, and popping back up to briefly unload the bar. Drive yourself underneath the bar, elevating it overhead as you descend into a full squat.
3. Return to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Heaving_Snatch_Balance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Heavy Bag Thrust', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Utilize a heavy bag for cet exercice. Assume an upright stance next to the bag, with vos pieds staggered, fairly wide apart. Place your hand on the bag at about poitrine height. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by twisting at the waist, pushing the bag forward as hard as possible. Perform this move quickly, pushing the bag away from votre corps.
3. Receive the bag as it swings back by reversing these steps.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Heavy_Bag_Thrust/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('High Cable Curls', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Stand between a couple of high pulleys and grab a handle in each arm. Position your upper arms in a way that they are parallèle au sol with the palms of vos mains facing you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Curl the handles towards you until they are next to your ears. Make sure that as you do so you flex your biceps and expirez. The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Maintenez la position 1 seconde in the contracted position as you squeeze the biceps.
3. Lentement, bring back the arms to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/High_Cable_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hip Circles (prone)', 'Abducteurs', 'Poids de corps', '1. Position yourself on vos mains and genous on the ground. Maintaining good posture, raise one bent genou off of the ground. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping the genou in a bent position, rotate the femur in an arc, attempting to make a big circle with your genou.
3. Perform this Lentement, for a number of repetitions, and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Hip_Circles_prone/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Hip Extension with Bands', 'Fessiers', 'Élastique', '1. Secure one end of the band to the lower portion of a post and attach the other to one cheville.
2. Facing the attachment point of the band, hold on to the column to stabilize yourself.
